---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<Section
  id="agents"
  title="Your agent tails the server you started in another terminal."
  more={{ href: '/agents/', label: 'More about agents' }}
>
  <p>
    The daemon owns the processes, so the agent's shell reaches the stack you started in yours: it
    tails the logs and restarts a service. On its own branch it gets its own lane, and its shell can
    end without the stack dying.
  </p>
  <Terminal slot="visual" title="agent session">
    <div class="chat">
      <p class="chat-you">checkout 500s on my lane 1, see what the api says</p>
      <div class="chat-agent">
        <pre><span class="command">devlanes logs myapp@1:api --tail 100</span>
<span class="failure">TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'id')</span>
    at createOrder (src/checkout/order.ts:48:31)
    at POST /checkout (src/routes/checkout.ts:19:5)</pre>
        <p>
          Guest checkout has no <code>cart.customer</code>, and <code>order.ts:48</code> reads{' '}
          <code>.id</code> off it. Added the guard, restarting api.
        </p>
        <pre><span class="dim">edited src/checkout/order.ts</span>
<span class="command">devlanes restart myapp@1:api</span>
<span class="success">ready</span> api  <span class="url">https://api.myapp1.localhost</span></pre>
        <p>
          Checkout answers again on <span class="url">https://myapp1.localhost</span>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Terminal>
</Section>
